{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Say to Aaron.</b> Because the Nile protected Moses when he was cast into it, therefore it was not struck through him — neither in blood nor in frogs — but was struck through Aaron (Shemot Rabbah)." "<b>Your streams.</b> These are flowing rivers, like our own rivers." "<b>Their canals.</b> These are channels that flow, made by human hands from the bank of the river to the fields; and the waters of the Nile collect and rise through the canals and irrigate the fields." "<b>Their ponds.</b> A gathering of waters that does not gush forth and does not flow, but stands in one place; and they call it אשטנ״ק." "<b>Throughout all the land of Egypt.</b> Even in the bathhouses and in the basins in the houses." "<b>And in the wood and in the stone.</b> The water in wooden vessels and in stone vessels."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {3 "The la'az אשטנ״ק is Old French estanc, 'pond, stagnant pool.'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:03.523761849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}